Table full name: isb-cgc-bq.CPTAC.copy_number_gene_level_hg38_gdc_current
Column name: primary_site Type: STRING Description: Anatomical site of the cancer under investigation or review
Column name: sample_barcode Type: STRING Description: TCGA sample barcode, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A. One sample may have multiple sets of CN segmentations corresponding to multiple aliquots; use GROUP BY appropriately in queries
Column name: gene_name Type: STRING Description: Gene name eg. TTN, DDR1
Column name: copy_number Type: INT64 Description: The weighted median of the strand copy numbers. Gene-level copy number data is generated by intersection of copy number segment and gene ranges. It is possible for one gene to overlap with multiple segments, and in this case, copy_number, min_copy_number and max_copy_number could take different values. In particular, the copy_number value is calculated as the median, weighted on length of overlapped bases, of segment copy numbers from all overlapped segments.
Sample rows:
[{'primary_site': 'Kidney', 'sample_barcode': 'C3N-01651-01', 'gene_name': 'AC104454.2'}, {'primary_site': 'Kidney', 'sample_barcode': 'C3N-01651-01', 'gene_name': 'AL137792.1'}, {'primary_site': 'Kidney', 'sample_barcode': 'C3N-01651-01', 'gene_name': 'PPIEL'}, {'primary_site': 'Kidney', 'sample_barcode': 'C3N-01651-01', 'gene_name': 'HSPE1P24'}, {'primary_site': 'Kidney', 'sample_barcode': 'C3N-01651-01', 'gene_name': 'RSL24D1P4'}]

